{"content_hash": "c38685545b6b784f", "version_id": 164, "article_id": 17, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "How the Nature Index Tables Are Built for 2026", "title_zh": "2026年自然指数榜单是怎么做出来的", "topic": "science", "source": "nature", "source_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02999-z", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52462408254_7688613222_b.jpg", "credit": "DCHNwam · pdm 1.0 · via flickr"}, "published_date": "2026-10-07", "word_count": 218, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "The 2026 Nature Spotlight on infectious diseases uses a special ranking system. Here is how the tables were created and what data they are based on.", "lead_zh": "2026年《自然》传染病专题采用了一套特别的排名方法。本文介绍这些榜单是如何制作的，以及它们依据的是什么数据。", "preview": "The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases are based on the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious d", "preview_zh": "2026年《自然》传染病专题的榜单基于自然指数数据库。它们涵盖2021年至2025年间发表在自然科学和健康科学期刊上的传染病文章。这意味着排名只包含这五年期间的研究。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 154, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/audio/17/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 92.45, "size_bytes": 558576, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 241, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ab49ecc/content/data/versions/164.json", "paragraphs": ["The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases are based on the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious diseases that were published in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025. This means the ranking only includes research from a five-year period.", "To find the right articles, a keyword search was carried out on titles and abstracts. The search used Digital Science's Dimensions database. Digital Science is part of Holtzbrinck, which is the majority shareholder of Springer Nature, the publisher of Nature. The search covered 83 infectious diseases and included five subcategories for severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes.", "The diseases and their search strings were the same as those used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious disease. Articles found in Dimensions that were also listed in the Nature Index database formed the final data set for the tables. This article is part of the Spotlight, which is an editorially independent supplement, and advertisers have no influence over its content.", "The related articles in the Spotlight explore several urgent topics. They ask whether the world can still end AIDS, why proper care is needed on the Ebola frontlines, and why strong science alone is not enough for pandemic preparedness. Other pieces look at drug-resistant bacteria, RNA vaccines, and the shifting burden of infectious disease in China."], "paragraphs_zh": ["2026年《自然》传染病专题的榜单基于自然指数数据库。它们涵盖2021年至2025年间发表在自然科学和健康科学期刊上的传染病文章。这意味着排名只包含这五年期间的研究。", "为了找到合适的文章，研究人员对标题和摘要进行了关键词搜索。搜索使用的是Digital Science旗下的Dimensions数据库。Digital Science是Holtzbrinck集团的一部分，而Holtzbrinck是《自然》的出版商施普林格·自然的多数股东。搜索覆盖了83种传染病，并包含五个子类别，涉及严重冠状病毒和流感亚型。", "这些疾病及其搜索字符串与2021年自然指数传染病专题所用的相同。在Dimensions中找到、同时也在自然指数数据库中的文章，构成了榜单的最终数据集。本文是专题的一部分，该专题是编辑独立的增刊，广告商对其内容没有影响。", "专题中的相关文章探讨了几个紧迫话题。它们提出：世界还能否终结艾滋病？为什么埃博拉疫情前线需要适当的护理？以及为什么仅靠强大的科学不足以做好大流行防范。其他文章关注耐药细菌、RNA疫苗以及中国传染病负担的变化。"], "body": "The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases are based on the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious diseases that were published in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025. This means the ranking only includes research from a five-year period.\n\nTo find the right articles, a keyword search was carried out on titles and abstracts. The search used Digital Science's Dimensions database. Digital Science is part of Holtzbrinck, which is the majority shareholder of Springer Nature, the publisher of Nature. The search covered 83 infectious diseases and included five subcategories for severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes.\n\nThe diseases and their search strings were the same as those used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious disease. Articles found in Dimensions that were also listed in the Nature Index database formed the final data set for the tables. This article is part of the Spotlight, which is an editorially independent supplement, and advertisers have no influence over its content.\n\nThe related articles in the Spotlight explore several urgent topics. They ask whether the world can still end AIDS, why proper care is needed on the Ebola frontlines, and why strong science alone is not enough for pandemic preparedness. Other pieces look at drug-resistant bacteria, RNA vaccines, and the shifting burden of infectious disease in China.", "body_zh": "2026年《自然》传染病专题的榜单基于自然指数数据库。它们涵盖2021年至2025年间发表在自然科学和健康科学期刊上的传染病文章。这意味着排名只包含这五年期间的研究。\n\n为了找到合适的文章，研究人员对标题和摘要进行了关键词搜索。搜索使用的是Digital Science旗下的Dimensions数据库。Digital Science是Holtzbrinck集团的一部分，而Holtzbrinck是《自然》的出版商施普林格·自然的多数股东。搜索覆盖了83种传染病，并包含五个子类别，涉及严重冠状病毒和流感亚型。\n\n这些疾病及其搜索字符串与2021年自然指数传染病专题所用的相同。在Dimensions中找到、同时也在自然指数数据库中的文章，构成了榜单的最终数据集。本文是专题的一部分，该专题是编辑独立的增刊，广告商对其内容没有影响。\n\n专题中的相关文章探讨了几个紧迫话题。它们提出：世界还能否终结艾滋病？为什么埃博拉疫情前线需要适当的护理？以及为什么仅靠强大的科学不足以做好大流行防范。其他文章关注耐药细菌、RNA疫苗以及中国传染病负担的变化。", "text": "The tables for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases are based on the Nature Index database. They cover articles about infectious diseases that were published in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025. This means the ranking only includes research from a five-year period. To find the right articles, a keyword search was carried out on titles and abstracts. The search used Digital Science's Dimensions database. Digital Science is part of Holtzbrinck, which is the majority shareholder of Springer Nature, the publisher of Nature. The search covered 83 infectious diseases and included five subcategories for severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes. The diseases and their search strings were the same as those used for the Nature Index 2021 Infectious disease. Articles found in Dimensions that were also listed in the Nature Index database formed the final data set for the tables. This article is part of the Spotlight, which is an editorially independent supplement, and advertisers have no influence over its content. The related articles in the Spotlight explore several urgent topics. They ask whether the world can still end AIDS, why proper care is needed on the Ebola frontlines, and why strong science alone is not enough for pandemic preparedness. Other pieces look at drug-resistant bacteria, RNA vaccines, and the shifting burden of infectious disease in China.", "vocab": [{"word": "infectious disease", "pos": "noun", "zh": "传染病", "note": "常用医学词汇，指由病原体引起的疾病。"}, {"word": "database", "pos": "noun", "zh": "数据库", "note": "指有组织地存储数据的系统。"}, {"word": "abstract", "pos": "noun", "zh": "摘要", "note": "学术论文开头的简短总结。"}, {"word": "methodology", "pos": "noun", "zh": "方法论；方法", "note": "指研究或操作所采用的一套方法。"}, {"word": "ranking", "pos": "noun", "zh": "排名", "note": "指按某种标准排列的名次。"}, {"word": "subcategory", "pos": "noun", "zh": "子类别", "note": "在大类别下进一步划分的小类。"}, {"word": "publisher", "pos": "noun", "zh": "出版商", "note": "负责出版书籍、期刊等的公司或机构。"}, {"word": "shareholder", "pos": "noun", "zh": "股东", "note": "持有公司股份的人或机构。"}, {"word": "supplement", "pos": "noun", "zh": "增刊；副刊", "note": "报纸或杂志额外出版的部分。"}, {"word": "advertiser", "pos": "noun", "zh": "广告商", "note": "付费投放广告的公司或个人。"}, {"word": "pandemic preparedness", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "大流行防范", "note": "为应对全球性疾病暴发所做的准备。"}, {"word": "drug-resistant", "pos": "adj", "zh": "耐药的", "note": "形容细菌等对药物不再敏感。"}], "title_original": "A guide to Nature Index tables", "summary_original": "Nature, Published online: 07 October 2026;\ndoi:10.1038/d41586-026-02999-z\nInformation on the methodology used in the ranking for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases.", "body_original": "SPOTLIGHT\n07 October 2026\nA guide to Nature Index tables\nInformation on the methodology used in the ranking for the 2026 Nature Spotlight: Infectious diseases.\nEmail\nBluesky\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nReddit\nWhatsapp\nX\nSave article\nView saved research\nThe tables for the 2026\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\nare based on the\nNature Index database\nand cover infectious-disease articles published in natural-science and health-science journals between 2021 and 2025.\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\nA keyword search on abstracts and titles was conducted to extract infectious-disease articles in Digital Science’s Dimensions database (Digital Science is part of Holtzbrinck, the majority shareholder of\nNature\n’s publisher, Springer Nature). The search covered 83 infectious diseases and included 5 subcategories to cover severe coronaviruses and influenza subtypes. The\ndiseases and their Dimensions search strings\nwere the same as those for\nNature Index 2021 Infectious disease\n. The Dimensions articles identified that were also in the Nature Index database formed the data set for the tables in this Spotlight.\nEnjoying our latest content?\nLog in or create an account to continue\nAccess the most recent journalism from Nature's award-winning team\nExplore the latest features & opinion covering groundbreaking research\nAccess through your institution\nor\nSign in or create an account\nContinue with Google\nContinue with ORCiD\ndoi: https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-02999-z\nThis article is part of\nNature Spotlight: Infectious diseases\n, an editorially independent supplement. Advertisers have no influence over the content.\nRelated Articles\n‘When prevention disappears, infections rise’: can the world still end AIDS?\nWhy we must advocate for proper care on the frontlines of the Ebola outbreak\nWhy sound, strong science alone isn’t enough in pandemic preparedness\nPartner content: The microbial sleuths tracking the rise of drug resistant bacteria\nPartner content: Investigating the next generation of RNA vaccines\nPartner content: The burden of infectious disease in China is shifting\nPartner content: Preparing for the next major disease outbreak\nPartner content: Big hospital, bigger ideas for pandemic preparedness\nPartner content: Zika research points the way to flavivirus antivirals\nSubjects\nDiseases\nInfection\nPublic health\nLatest on:\nDiseases\nInfection\nPublic health\nWhy sound, strong science alone isn’t enough in pandemic preparedness\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nWhy we must advocate for proper care on the frontlines of the Ebola outbreak\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nRevealed: how this common gut microbe protects against heart disease\nNews\n07 OCT 26\nFlu season could kick off ‘incredibly’ early — what scientists are watching\nNews\n06 OCT 26\n‘Epigenetic’ editing is here: gene-tagging technique banishes hepatitis B virus\nNews\n21 SEP 26\n‘Stomach bugs’ send protective immune cells rushing from gut to brain\nNews\n15 SEP 26\n‘When prevention disappears, infections rise’: can the world still end AIDS?\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nWhy sound, strong science alone isn’t enough in pandemic preparedness\nSpotlight\n07 OCT 26\nFlu season could kick off ‘incredibly’ early — what scientists are watching\nNews\n06 OCT 26\nJobs\nFaculty Positions at the Center for Machine Learning Research (CMLR), Peking University\nCMLR's goal is to advance machine learning-related research across a wide range of disciplines.\nBeijing (CN)\nCenter for Machine Learning Research (CMLR), Peking University\nAssistant or Associate Professor of Cell Biology\nDepartment of Cell Biology at the University of Virginia School of Medicine invites applications for Assistant or Associate Professor of Cell Biology\nCharlottesville, Virginia\nUniversity of Virginia\nRecruitment Announcement for High-Level Talent at the Center for Agricultural Microbiology\nJoin HZAU's global faculty team to advance research with competitive benefits.\nWuhan, Hubei (CN)\nHuazhong Agricultu